Description: Announce the unlock in WlSessionLock::unlock()
 WlSessionLock::unlock() released the lock through SessionLockManager::unlock(),
 which clears the lock object, and only then checked isLocked() to decide
 whether to emit lockStateChanged. isLocked() was false by then, so unlocking
 never announced the change: a QML binding on WlSessionLock.locked kept its
 locked value, and Omarchy's lock service, which reads such a binding before
 starting a lock, took the session for still locked and never locked it
 again until the shell restarted. Read the state before releasing it.
 .
 Seen on Oaxaca 2026-10-15 (Quickshell 0.3.2): the first lock after login
 worked, every later one did nothing; the lock service's log showed
 "secure=false" on unlock but no "session-locked=false". The same code is
 on Quickshell's master branch (2026-10-15).
Author: Oaxaca maintainers
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-15
---
--- a/src/wayland/session_lock.cpp
+++ b/src/wayland/session_lock.cpp
@@ -172,6 +172,9 @@
 
 void WlSessionLock::unlock() {
 	this->lockTarget = false;
+	// Read before releasing: SessionLockManager::unlock() clears the lock, so isLocked() is
+	// false afterwards and the change was never announced.
+	auto wasLocked = this->isLocked();
 
 	for (auto* surface: this->surfaces) {
 		surface->deleteLater();
@@ -180,7 +183,7 @@
 	this->surfaces.clear();
 
 	if (this->manager) this->manager->unlock();
-	if (this->isLocked()) emit this->lockStateChanged();
+	if (wasLocked) emit this->lockStateChanged();
 }
 
 void WlSessionLock::onScreensChanged() {
